      "content": "I get the \"moving target\" angle, but they're super data-driven. If I go in there talking about \"unforeseen threats\" without being able to point to any specific vulnerabilities or recent close calls in their logs, they're gonna call my bluff. Is there anything in the audit—even if it's just a minor thing—that we can highlight as a specific weakness to justify the need for constant monitoring? We really need a concrete hook to get this signed.",
